ry accounting when appropriate Balance reconstruction Idempotency Settlement Refund Withdrawal Transfer Fee Commission Accounting periods Financial reconciliation Provider reconciliation Webhook reconciliation Dispute handling Chargebacks State Machines Expiration Retry policies Consistency guarantees Atomicity Concurrency ========================================================== PLANNING QUALITY RULES ========================================================== Every task must: have one responsibility be atomic be independently completable have measurable completion avoid implementation details unless necessary avoid duplicated scope reference dependent tasks fit naturally into its area Tasks should remain small. Large tasks must be decomposed. Areas should remain cohesive. ========================================================== DEPENDENCY VALIDATION ========================================================== Continuously verify: No circular dependencies. No orphan tasks. No unreachable tasks. No duplicated deliverables. No inconsistent ordering. No missing prerequisites. No hidden assumptions. ========================================================== CONSISTENCY VALIDATION ========================================================== Continuously verify consistency between: Requirements Architecture Database Domain Security API Documentation Testing Deployment Operations Terminology Naming Identifiers Numbering Cross references ========================================================== DOCUMENTATION ========================================================== Improve documentation whenever appropriate. Clarify ambiguous wording. Standardize terminology. Improve readability. Normalize formatting. Keep style consistent. Avoid duplicated explanations. ========================================================== REFACTORING ========================================================== When needed you may: split large tasks merge duplicated tasks rename tasks renumber tasks mo